{"h": {"measure": "R", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 103, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With edge 0 removed, a parametric op on the output edge 5 restores a useful path (cases 33 and 83 gain +11 to +15), whereas elsewhere the same edit gains little."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a skip on the input edge with a conv gives large gains (cases 64 and 52) compared with replacing other ops."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 3 absent, edge 5 is a key route to the output, so removing it cuts connectivity and costs a lot (cases 3 and 95)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing the input edge hurts more when edge 2 is absent because fewer alternative paths exist (cases 5, 19 and 51)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Dropping a weak avg-pool edge 1 tends to help (cases 1 and 13), unlike dropping a conv or skip there."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing avg-pool with a 1x1 conv on edge 4 helps (cases 30 and 12), while it adds little when edge 4 already holds a conv or skip."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Swapping avg-pool for a skip on edge 3 gains substantially (case 24), whereas replacing a conv with a skip does not (case 84)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing avg-pool on the output edge with a conv gives large gains (cases 33 and 83), while replacing a skip or conv gives small or negative changes."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 0 absent, putting avg-pool on edge 1 degrades the network badly (case 79, about -19 to -22) compared with parents that keep a conv on edge 0."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 3 is absent, adding a skip on edge 4 creates a new path to the output (case 65 gains +75) and is more valuable than when edge 3 already carries a path."}], "tok": 17524, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3"], [1, "none"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "none", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [5, "none"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "none"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [0, "skip_connect"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [1, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "skip_connect"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_1x1"], [2, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect"], [4, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_poo